1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,820
California has a chance to elect someone who has had the lived experiences, who represents Californians, and who can be a voice that is not represented and won't be represented in the Senate.

2
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:16,660
It is important that an elected official understand the daily lives of people.

3
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:21,160
Here in California, for example, 40 million people living one paycheck away from poverty.

4
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:29,780
I was on public assistance, food stamps, raised two single little boys as a single mother, had to take them to class because I couldn't afford child care.

5
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:35,880
I've worked as a community worker with the Black Panther Party, so I know what activism means.

6
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:37,720
I was a target of COINTELPRO.

7
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:42,380
I know how the FBI came and tried to destroy the Black Panther Party.

8
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:45,960
So it's lived experiences none of the other candidates have had.

9
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:56,840
And so I want to be that voice, that lens, that perspective that's badly needed in the United States Senate so I can be the voice of people in California to make life better for everybody.

